From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 20:43:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j713: name the SEP's domain
 in the PMGR policy

The boot-time PMGR policy now resolves on the Air, and it disabled the
domain, as it's the board's tree that names it. The SEP driver then
timed out waiting for its power domains, and every deep sleep was
refused with the enclave still running.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit ea54a3ea1d0c6e28d31ec22171ea8803d77ee87d)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi | 6 ------
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi | 4 +++-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi
index e4e5e7c10b..62207f9f63 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-j715.dtsi
@@ -142,12 +142,6 @@ &sep_dart {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-/* Only named: the sleep's last refusal reads its state to see the enclave gate. */
-&ps_sep {
-	apple,firmware-owned;
-	status = "okay";
-};
-
 &sep {
 	/*
 	 * Without a domain the driver tells the enclave at .suspend, and a sleep
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi
index d9bc2dfff4..75a9273e6e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j713-pmgr.dtsi
@@ -445,8 +445,10 @@ &ps_avd_sys {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* Only named: the sleep's last refusal reads its state to see the enclave gate. */
 &ps_sep {
-	status = "disabled";
+	apple,firmware-owned;
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &ps_isp_cpu {
-- 
